      "writtenOn": "2023-09-07T08:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC this should be nullable (there is no constraint that there is a single ancestor to all states in the state machine, or said another way, null is the top node of the tree). As this is recursive, it will end up called with null by l.212. E.g. :\n\n- Add two states State1 and State2 both with null as parent\n- Start in State1\n- `performTransitions()` to State2\n- `commonAncestor \u003d null` in l.191\n- `executeExitMethods(null, State1)`\n- State1.exit() and State1.mActive \u003d false\n- `executeExitMethods(null, null)`\n\nEventually this doesn\u0027t crash and even behaves as expected because null \u003d\u003d null in l.207. However the annotation is wrong.",
